      "writtenOn": "2026-09-06T21:40:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can be true for devices with multiple components as well. Is this intentional, since your commit message calls out only single compoennt FDs?",
      "revId": "0c93b53a3ae32faca5449009e7dc42b002047832",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3dac8dd0_52765bb2",
        "filename": "fw-update/inventory_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 705,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002484
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-09T07:04:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this is intentional. The check is deliberately generic: it keys on version-string equality, not on component count. A multi-component FD whose image set version happens to equal one of its component versions has exactly the same redundancy, so suppressing the duplicate there is equally correct. Single-component FDs are called out in the commit message because they hit this by construction (the image set version is always the same as the only component\u0027s version), i.e. they\u0027re the motivating case rather than a restriction.",
      "parentUuid": "671c3567_ec55d03b",
      "revId": "0c93b53a3ae32faca5449009e7dc42b002047832",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
